    "updated_at": "2026-09-05T14:19:34Z",
    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #258\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed to branch `bb/relay-99-mailbox-experience-07-07-trigger-agent-thr_gbmjzw5n7i`.\n\nImplements issue #99: registers a `newEmail` heartbeat on the Emails database (`onItemEvent`, `create`), dispatched through the existing `core.agentRun` action — no separate mail scheduler. A new generic `itemRelationFilter` on `core.agentRun`'s `actionConfig` gates the run on the fired item's folder relations, evaluated at fire time (after the folder-membership relation, written later in the same ingest transaction, has committed):\n\n- Requires at least one related Folder with `specialPurpose = \"inbox\"`.\n- Excludes the message if any related Folder has `specialPurpose` in `junk`/`trash` — including messages with multiple folder memberships (e.g. Gmail-style labels).\n- Dedup for reconciliation needs no new code: `ingestEmailMessage`'s existing Message-ID convergence only calls `createItemWithClient` (the sole trigger point for the `create` event) for genuinely new messages, so a resynced/already-known message never re-fires the event.\n\nNew test file `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/newEmailHeartbeat.test.ts` covers: one event for new Inbox mail, zero for junk/trash-only mail, zero for mail in both Inbox and Junk, and no duplicate event on reconciliation of an already-known message.\n\nVerified: full backend build (`pnpm -r run build`, 7 packages) and the complete backend test suite (16 files, 227 tests) pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
